if the two ever differ, this License applies.

## 1. Purpose

Apsi is free to use, and its source code is open so that anyone can learn from it, build with it and improve it.
This License keeps three promises at the same time:

1. **Anyone may use Apsi for any purpose**, including at work, in companies, in government and in products they
   sell, without paying.
2. **Nobody may sell Apsi itself**, or charge for access to Apsi itself, without a separate written licence from
   ATEC. Changed versions of Apsi stay available under this License.
3. **The origin is always credited** to ATEC.

## 2. Definitions

**"Software"** means the Apsi programming language implementation that ATEC publishes under this License: its
compiler, interpreter, runtime, standard library, command-line tools, editor extensions, installers, documentation,
examples and website source code, and any part of them, in source or compiled form.

**"Modified Version"** means a work that contains the Software or a substantial part of it, changed or not,
including forks, ports, translations into another language, and works that are based on the Software's source code.
A Modified Version does not include Your Programs.

**"Your Programs"** means anything You create *with* the Software rather than *from* it: programs and libraries
written in the Apsi language, programs converted to Apsi with `apsi convert`, models You train, data, files and
other results Your programs produce, and executables made from Your programs with `apsi build`.

**"Runtime Copy"** means an unmodified copy of the Software's runtime and standard library that is included in, or
installed together with, one of Your Programs so that it can run (for example inside an executable made with
`apsi build`, a container image, or an installer of Your application).

**"Selling the Software"** means any of the following, done for money or other compensation:

1. selling, renting, sublicensing or charging for copies of the Software or a Modified Version;
2. charging for downloading, installing or accessing the Software or a Modified Version, or placing it behind a
   paywall or a paid account;
3. offering the Software or a Modified Version to third parties as a hosted service — for example a paid online
   Apsi compiler, notebook, playground, IDE, API or package registry — where the Software provides a substantial
   part of what the customer pays for;
4. selling a product whose main value is the Software or a Modified Version itself, such as a paid distribution,
   a paid plug-in that unlocks parts of the Software, or a paid language or compiler built from the Software.

Selling the Software does **not** include: selling or running Your Programs (with Runtime Copies); using the
Software inside an organisation; charging for Your own work, such as development, consulting, teaching, training,
support or hosting of Your Programs; or receiving donations, grants or sponsorship.

**"You"** means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this License. For a legal entity, "You" includes
every entity that controls it, is controlled by it, or is under common control with it.

## 3. Licence granted to You

Subject to the conditions of this License, ATEC grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence, for as
long as the copyright lasts, to:

1. **use** the Software for any purpose, commercial or not, including running it in production;
2. **study** the source code and **modify** it;
3. **make and distribute copies** of the Software and of Modified Versions, free of charge;
4. **create, use, sell and distribute Your Programs**, including with Runtime Copies;
5. **analyse** the Software with any tool, including automated analysis and the training of machine-learning
   models. Distributing a substantial part of the Software's code, also when a model reproduces it, is distribution
   under this License.

## 4. Patent licence

ATEC grants You a licence under every patent claim it can license that would be infringed by using the Software as
ATEC published it, for the purposes allowed in section 3. If You, or an entity acting on Your behalf, start a legal
claim alleging that the Software infringes a patent, this patent licence ends on the date the claim is filed.

## 5. Conditions

### 5.1 Do not sell the Software

You may not engage in Selling the Software without a separate written licence from ATEC (section 11). This applies
to the Software and to every Modified Version.

### 5.2 Credit

Every copy of the Software and every Modified Version that You distribute, in source or compiled form, must:

1. keep this License and all copyright, licence and attribution notices intact;
2. say, where users will see it (for example in the README, the "about" screen or the documentation), that it is
   based on Apsi, originally developed by ATEC, with the address https://github.com/ATECTechnologies/apsi;
3. say that it was changed, if it was, and by whom.

For Your Programs that include a Runtime Copy, a one-line credit in the program's documentation, licence file or
"about" information is enough: `Uses the Apsi runtime by ATEC (https://apsi.dev), Apsi License 2.0.`

Credit may not be hidden, removed or made misleading.

### 5.3 Modified Versions stay under this License

Modified Versions may be distributed only under this License, with sections 5.1 to 5.4 unchanged, and with their
source code available to the people who receive them at no charge. You may not add terms that take away rights this
License gives. This condition does not apply to Your Programs, which You may license as You choose.

### 5.4 Names and logo

This License does not grant rights to the names "Apsi" and "ATEC" or to the Apsi logo, except to state truthfully
where a work comes from as section 5.2 requires. You may not suggest that ATEC endorses, sponsors or certifies You
or Your work. A Modified Version must not be presented as the official Apsi; give it a name of its own (for example
"X, based on Apsi"). Your Programs may say that they are written in Apsi.

## 6. What stays Yours

Your Programs and everything they produce belong to You. ATEC claims no rights in them, and this License places no
conditions on them other than the credit for a Runtime Copy in section 5.2.

